  "pd": {
    "basis": "author-died-pre-1930",
    "detail": "Angel Gregorio Villoldo (1868-1919) died more than 95 years ago; El Choclo was premiered in 1903 at the restaurant El Americano in Buenos Aires and printed shortly after, so it is free worldwide.",
    "sourceEdition": "Villoldo, 'El Choclo', early Buenos Aires piano editions; read through a public-domain ABC transcription of the original first and second strains",
    "notes": "Melody and harmony only, never lyrics: the familiar Spanish words are Discepolo (1947) and the English Kiss of Fire lyric is 1952, both separate later works in their own copyright, and neither is carried here. Written in 2/4 with 16th-note figures and encoded as 4/4 with each written bar becoming one encoded bar and every value doubled, the standard cut-time mapping. The third strain modulates to A major, so it is left out to keep the whole song in one mode. Tango is straight and marcato, never swung."
  },
